{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies","id":1090106,"title":"Temporal Sympathy For Dummies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-08T21:10:18-07:00","id":1090106,"title":"Temporal Sympathy For Dummies","content":"Can someone explain to me Temporal Sympathy in a way even an idiot like me can understand it? Like when do I need it? How do I determine the penalty?<br /> <br /> Examples would be amazing if you can manage it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-08T21:40:44-07:00","id":1090114,"title":"","content":"Temporal sympathy is a measure of how similar a subject is now to how they were at a given point in their history; like the connections that Space magic deals with, lower degrees of similarity make it harder to close the gap between those two eras, but such ties are easier to meddle with.<br /> <br /> You need it when you're casting a Time spell that draws forth a piece of the subject's past, casts them backward along the timeline of their own experience, or otherwise makes targeted observations or alterations to their history \u2014 such as using Temporal Summoning to restore an elderly master to their prime, looking into the past of a ruin to see what it was like when it was inhabited, or stepping into your own childhood to change the course of your life. You also need it in a way that scales in the opposite direction if you want to alter a subject's temporal sympathies \u2014 strengthening a building's sympathy with the period where it housed a restaurant to bolster a business venture, for instance.<br /> <br /> You determine the Withstand rating by referencing the chart at the start of the Time Arcanum writeup and comparing what the target is like now to the point in its history that you're looking for \u2014 if I want to get back to the day before I last renewed my driver's license, I'd be advised to make plans to renew my driver's license in a few days and try to replicate as much of the other events and emotions surrounding that day as possible to strengthen the resemblance. (This isn't always a simple or easy task, particularly if you're angling for a time in your life that was several age bands back from your current age, like shooting for the teenage years from the vantage of a great-grandparent, but the general principle applies if you aren't using magic to move the connection strength up.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:17:09-07:00","id":1090139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies?p=1090114#post1090114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Temporal sympathy is a measure of how similar a subject is now to how they were at a given point in their history; like the connections that Space magic deals with, lower degrees of similarity make it harder to close the gap between those two eras, but such ties are easier to meddle with.<br /> <br /> You need it when you're casting a Time spell that draws forth a piece of the subject's past, casts them backward along the timeline of their own experience, or otherwise makes targeted observations or alterations to their history \u2014 such as using Temporal Summoning to restore an elderly master to their prime, looking into the past of a ruin to see what it was like when it was inhabited, or stepping into your own childhood to change the course of your life. You also need it in a way that scales in the opposite direction if you want to alter a subject's temporal sympathies \u2014 strengthening a building's sympathy with the period where it housed a restaurant to bolster a business venture, for instance.<br /> <br /> You determine the Withstand rating by referencing the chart at the start of the Time Arcanum writeup and comparing what the target is like now to the point in its history that you're looking for \u2014 if I want to get back to the day before I last renewed my driver's license, I'd be advised to make plans to renew my driver's license in a few days and try to replicate as much of the other events and emotions surrounding that day as possible to strengthen the resemblance. (This isn't always a simple or easy task, particularly if you're angling for a time in your life that was several age bands back from your current age, like shooting for the teenage years from the vantage of a great-grandparent, but the general principle applies if you aren't using magic to move the connection strength up.)</div> </div> </div> </div>What are you talking about. What has trying to replicate as much of the other events and emotions surrounding that day have to do with anything? Why are you making it complicated?<br /> <br /> The only thing that matters is how much the thing/person/place has changed since the time you want to target. If you changed your driving license yesterday you have a strong temporal sympathy, if you changed it 10 years ago you have a weak temporal sympathy.<br /> <br /> Emotions, replicating events dont mean anything. You cant dress up as your teenage self and smoke week because that is what you were doing 10 years ago when you last renewed your drivers license to make it easier...(well you could, that might be the yantra needed but it wont effect the links strength)<br /> <br /> Basically Bloodyquill, think to yourself. How has this place/thing/person changed since the time i want to target, and use the chart on page 186 to guide you. Nobody will slap you if you get it wrong the first few times, also i like to ask my players what they think the sympathy is get everybodys input if i cant make up my mind,<br /> <br /> A street corner might not have changed much in a year since the local pet shop closed. Sure different people walk up and down every day and small changes have happened but its still pretty much the same place day in day out. If somebody breaks a window one day though, thats a change that might weaken your sympathy to the time before it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1534,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","user":"totalgit","date":". 05-09-2017, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:32:42-07:00","id":1090152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies?p=1090139#post1090139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What are you talking about. What has trying to replicate as much of the other events and emotions surrounding that day have to do with anything? Why are you making it complicated?<br /> <br /> The only thing that matters is how much the thing/person/place has changed since the time you want to target. If you changed your driving license yesterday you have a strong temporal sympathy, if you changed it 10 years ago you have a weak temporal sympathy.<br /> <br /> Emotions, replicating events dont mean anything. You cant dress up as your teenage self and smoke week because that is what you were doing 10 years ago when you last renewed your drivers license to make it easier...(well you could, that might be the yantra needed but it wont effect the links strength)</div> </div> </div> </div>I think he's talking about ways to strengthen Temporal Sympathy without magic, rather than preparations for using Temporal Sympathy, in that last paragraph.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T00:54:29-07:00","id":1090162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies?p=1090152#post1090152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think he's talking about ways to strengthen Temporal Sympathy without magic, rather than preparations for using Temporal Sympathy, in that last paragraph.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see that working for items/places, you can arrange them/restore them to as close as possible to the time your trying to target. People are a different kettle of fish i imagine, im nothing like my thin (weep) teenage self and no amount of trying to diet will help <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Maybe i was to harsh saying replicating stuff doesnt matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1534-totalgit","name":"totalgit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1534_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"742"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:33:46-07:00","id":1090295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>totalgit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies?p=1090139#post1090139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What are you talking about. What has trying to replicate as much of the other events and emotions surrounding that day have to do with anything? Why are you making it complicated?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because there's a reason temporal sympathy runs on a sliding scale based on change rather than a strict linear progression of Unchanged to Strong to Medium to Weak scaling directly with time.<br /> <br /> A picture of the artist at age 17 in a black turtleneck feeling alone at an isolated crossroads in the woods with a rusty sign at the fork is closer to a picture of the artist at age 48 in a black turtleneck feeling alone at an isolated crossroads in the woods with a rusty sign at the form than it is to a picture of the artist at age 48 in a red shirt feeling irritable at a busy downtown coffee shop with a brand new billboard out the window.<br /> <br /> That's not &quot;making it complicated,&quot; that's mundane use of basic sympathetic principles. If that infuriates you for some reason, I'm sorry to say I have no way of changing the way resemblance works.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T07:53:57-07:00","id":1090305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies?p=1090295#post1090295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because there's a reason temporal sympathy runs on a sliding scale based on change rather than a strict linear progression of Unchanged to Strong to Medium to Weak scaling directly with time.<br /> <br /> A picture of the artist at age 17 in a black turtleneck feeling alone at an isolated crossroads in the woods with a rusty sign at the fork is closer to a picture of the artist at age 48 in a black turtleneck feeling alone at an isolated crossroads in the woods with a rusty sign at the form than it is to a picture of the artist at age 48 in a red shirt feeling irritable at a busy downtown coffee shop with a brand new billboard out the window.<br /> <br /> That's not &amp;quot;making it complicated,&amp;quot; that's mundane use of basic sympathetic principles. If that infuriates you for some reason, I'm sorry to say I have no way of changing the way resemblance works.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure the example of pictures is a good one since you're one of the more insistent people that a thing only has temporal sympathy with itself and that's what we're talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T08:07:21-07:00","id":1090313,"title":"","content":"A picture is a Yantra and most likely provides no sympathetic connection. Surprisingly it would be better to find some picture of trains that your target took at that time. It will be more personal than a picture of him. Hand made objects, sculptures, poems, offspring, or a bumper of car that hit this poor guy contain sympathy. Picture is just a Yantra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T09:39:48-07:00","id":1090338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies?p=1090305#post1090305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure the example of pictures is a good one since you're one of the more insistent people that a thing only has temporal sympathy with itself and that's what we're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>For clarity, then: I'm talking about the imagery of related scenes, not sympathetic Yantras (photographic or otherwise). It's easier to get to times in a subject's existence that strongly resemble their current circumstances and harder to do so for ones that weakly resemble them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T09:53:42-07:00","id":1090341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies?p=1090338#post1090338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For clarity, then: I'm talking about the imagery of related scenes, not sympathetic Yantras (photographic or otherwise). It's easier to get to times in a subject's existence that strongly resemble their current circumstances and harder to do so for ones that weakly resemble them.</div> </div> </div> </div>So basically by modeling a time from an earlier temporal sympathy stage you actually lower the temporal sympathy withstand. Can you drop that all the way to Unchanged then?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-09T10:36:09-07:00","id":1090354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090106-temporal-sympathy-for-dummies?p=1090341#post1090341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So basically by modeling a time from an earlier temporal sympathy stage you actually lower the temporal sympathy withstand. Can you drop that all the way to Unchanged then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not without magical assistance or other supernatural weirdness or a very durable/resilient/easily-restored set of targets, just as Connected spatial sympathy is hard to come by naturally outside of very specific relationships, but in theory, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}